        "The data path is a pipeline, not a loop that waits. The client keeps up to W = 256 WRITEs outstanding in the SQ — the window — and posts them in linked lists of K = 64 WRs per ibv_post_send call, so one doorbell covers 64 WRITEs instead of one per WRITE.",
        "Only every K-th WRITE is signaled (generates a CQE). Because RC completions are in-order, one CQE accounts for exactly K WRITEs — completions are counted in exact multiples of K, and 256/64 = 4 CQEs cover the whole window.",
        "The refill discipline sits between lists: while the window is full, poll the CQEs that are ready and reclaim their slots; then post the next list immediately. The SQ never drains to zero, so the NIC never idles. Messages ≤ max_inline_data ride the WQE inline (IBV_SEND_INLINE); larger ones are DMA-read from the single registered 1 MB buffer.",
